 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **No Reliable Observations:** If a Gaussian has no reliable observations (e.g., in heavily occluded or texture-less regions), the consensus is undefined. The pseudocode handles this by setting consensus to zero and weights to zero, effectively ignoring the Gaussian in the VTC loss [G].
